## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design scalable, secure cross-account access with ephemeral credentials, tenant isolation, and proactive breach testing in a real-world multi-account data pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- IAM Roles Anywhere + OIDC for short-lived, tenant-scoped credentials
- Lake Formation per-tenant access controls
- Cross-account trust with least privilege
- CMK rotation and key policy governance
- Automated breach simulations, revocation, comprehensive auditing

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "kinesis:DescribeStream",
        "kinesis:GetRecords",
        "kinesis:GetShardIterator"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kinesis:account-a:region:stream/tenant-*-stream",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/TenantID": "${aws:username}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of IAM least-privilege, S3 encryption, presigned URLs, and rapid breach containment.

## Key Concepts
- Least-privilege IAM policies and role separation
- S3 server-side encryption with a KMS key
- Presigned URLs via STS for temporary read access
- Public access blocking at the bucket level
- Audit logging with CloudTrail; breach containment plan

## Code Example
```json
// Bucket policy (deny public access and allow app-specific principals)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}}
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// Lambda execution role trust (example)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test key rotation and ensure no downtime?
- What metrics would you monitor to detect misconfigurations or drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a zero-trust, per-tenant encryption and cross-account isolation architecture with advanced containment capabilities and hardware-level attestations.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC using tenant tags for granular cross-account access control
- Tenant-scoped CMKs with automated 90-day rotation and envelope encryption
- Nitro Enclaves attestations ensuring data-in-use protection via hardware isolation
- PrivateLink/VPC endpoints to eliminate public egress paths and enforce data residency
- 60-second containment workflow: automatic credential revocation, CMK rotation, and tenant quarantine
- Immutable auditing: CloudTrail with organizational trails, S3 Object Lock for WORM compliance, and Lake Formation for fine-grained data access logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example policy for tenant-scoped ABAC access
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::${AccountId}:role/EMR-Spark-Worker"
      },
      "Action": [
        "kms:Decrypt",
        "kms:GenerateDataKey"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:*:*:key/tenant-${TenantId}-*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "${TenantId}"
        },
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

